==Usage Notes==
* Jokers are usually obtained through [[the Shop]] or [[Booster Packs|Buffoon Packs]]. Other means include:
** Using the {{Tarot|Judgement}} [[Tarot card]], {{Spectral|The Soul}} or {{Spectral|Wraith}} [[Spectral card]] to create a Joker.
** {{J|Riff-Raff}} can create up to 2 common Jokers for each blind selected.
** {{Spectral|Ankh}} can create a copy of a random Joker, at the cost of destroying all other destructible Jokers. This means that {{Hl|sblue|Ankh}} can't destroy {{Sticker|Eternal}} Jokers.
** The {{Tag|Top-up}} can create up to 2 common Jokers if you have space. The {{Tag|Uncommon}} and {{Tag|Rare}} generate a random Joker of their respective rarity when entering [[the Shop]] or rerolling.
* A duplicate Joker cannot spawn during the run if it already exists on screen, unless the player has {{J|Showman}}.
** Exceptions to this are duplicating an already owned Joker by using {{Spectral|Ankh}} or {{J|Invisible Joker}}.
** If all unlocked Jokers of a specific rarity exist on the screen, every subsequent Joker instance of that rarity seen in the Shop or created using Joker generation (such as {{Tarot|Judgement}}) will be replaced by {{j|Joker}} (though this will never happen with Uncommon Jokers due to {{J|Showman}}).
* Retroactively adding modifiers to Jokers can only be done through {{Tarot|The Wheel of Fortune}}, {{Spectral|Ectoplasm}}, or {{Spectral|Hex}}.
** {{V|Hone}} and {{V|Glow Up}} make it more likely to find Jokers with editions in the [[The Shop|Shop]].
** Skipping a Blind for the {{Tag|Holographic}}, {{Tag|Polychrome}}, {{Tag|Negative}}, or {{Tag|Foil}} can guarantee an edition on a Joker in the next Shop.
* Joker slots begin at 5 most of the time, but there are exceptions and various ways to modify this.
** Purchasing {{V|Blank}}, and then {{V|Antimatter}} will let you gain +1 joker slot.
** {{D|Painted}} only starts with 4 joker slots. The {{D|Cruelty}} and {{D|Blast Off}} Challenge Decks reduce joker slots as well, to 3 and 4 respectively.
** {{D|Black}} has an additional joker slot, for a total of 6. The {{D|Five-Card Draw}} Challenge Deck also increases joker slots, to 7.
** Having {{Edition|Negative}} Jokers allows the player to have a Joker that gives an extra joker slot, essentially not taking up a slot.
* The {{D|Jokerless}} Challenge Deck bans all methods of obtaining jokers and sets joker slots to 0, making it impossible to use any. The {{D|Typecast}} Challenge Deck also sets joker slots to 0, but only after [[Ante 4]].
* The {{D|Bram Poker}} challenge prevents Jokers from appearing in the shop, although they can still be obtained by methods like {{Tarot|Judgement}}.
* Jokers, like every other purchasable consumable or playing card, only need to be purchased once to be "discovered", even if the action is cancelled by quitting and reloading the save.
** This can be taken advantage of by selling run-winning Jokers, then buying undiscovered ones, quitting to the Main Menu, and loading the run again to undo the purchase while still having new Jokers discovered for their collection.

== Trivia ==
* With the exception of [[Legendary Jokers]], all Joker art includes the word "Joker" (though it is obscured on {{J|Smeared Joker}}).
* Originally Balatro was only going to have 120 Jokers. This changed after a miscommunication with [[Playstack]] and LocalThunk discussing 150 Jokers, resulting in LocalThunk creating 30 more.<ref>{{ShortQuote|I once told Playstack (my publisher) that the full version of Balatro would have 120 Jokers. In a meeting later that week they mentioned something about '150 Jokers' and instead of correcting them I just made 30 more Jokers lmao|[[LocalThunk]]|[https://x.com/LocalThunk/status/1851133286363574286 on X/Twitter]}}</ref>
* Some jokers not present in the public release of Balatro have been revealed later, such as [[Obsolete content|Chaos Theory, the Toker, and Homework Eating Dog]].
* Most of the chip jokers have blue lips instead of the more default red lips.
* The average price of all Jokers is $6.14. If legendary Jokers are excluded, this falls to roughly $5.662.

